    {
      "title": "Spain announces plan to ease housing crisis amid outcry over eviction of 87-year-old",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/29/spanish-government-approves-measures-ease-housing-crisis-outcry-eviction",
      "description": "<p>Measures, which need to be approved in Congress, include extending ban on evictions of vulnerable people</p><p>Spain’s Socialist Workers’ party-led coalition government has approved a range of measures aimed at easing the country’s housing crisis, including extending a ban on evictions of vulnerable tenants until 2030, after <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/29/spain-madrid-tent-camp-housing-crisis\">a public outcry</a> over the eviction of an 87-year-old disabled woman from her Madrid apartment last week.</p><p>Two decrees have been approved by cabinet but will need to be approved in Congress, where the coalition lacks a majority. The government has requested a special parliamentary session on Friday in the hope of getting the decrees passed as soon as possible.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/29/spanish-government-approves-measures-ease-housing-crisis-outcry-eviction\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-29T14:27:03"
    },
    {
      "title": "Evicted Woman Set to Return Home as Spain Announces Plans to Fix Housing Crisis",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/29/world/europe/spain-housing-eviction-maricarmen-abascal-madrid-protests.html",
      "description": "The eviction of an 87-year-old set off protests in the country, which has an acute housing shortage. The government presented legislation to protect renters.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-09-29T15:06:48"
